          "filename": "Charing Cross Station (8200239816).jpg",
          "caption": "Charing Cross Station, 07/66. Built by the Charing Cross Railway in 1860, the CCR was taken over by the South Eastern Railway in 1864 which joined forces with the London, Chatham &amp; Dover Railway in 1899 to form the South Eastern &amp; Chatham Railway in 1899.The SECR became part of the Southern Railway in 1923 which became the Southern Region of Bristih Railways in 1948 upon Nationalisation.From left to right is \"4-CEP\" No.7209, \"4-EPB's\" No.5340 and 5310 and \"2-HAP\" No.6170.  \n\nScanned photograph taken with a Kowa SET camera.",
